# Living Survey: Artificial_General_Intelligence                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Introduction                                                                                                
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
This document collects the scientific literature regarding **Artificial_General_Intelligence**.                
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
## Recent Developments in AGI Research                                                                         
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Recent literature continues to explore the conceptual, architectural, and ethical dimensions of AGI. Policy    
discussions emphasize the need for conceptual discipline, particularly in high-stakes domains like healthcare, 
where the term AGI is often used ambiguously[^10.1016_j.jrt.2026.100183]. Concurrently, theoretical frameworks 
are proposing novel architectures for autonomous general intelligence, such as morphogenetic topologies that   
redefine the transition from computation to genuine                                                            
autonomy[^10.5281_zenodo.19034234][^10.5281_zenodo.19034233].                                                  
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
Safety and controllability remain central concerns, with recent proposals advocating for provably safe systems 
as the only viable path to controllable AGI, leveraging formal verification and mechanistic                    
interpretability[^10.48550_arxiv.2309.01933]. Ethical and sociopolitical critiques also highlight the risks of 
unregulated AGI development, linking certain normative frameworks to historical discriminatory practices and   
urging a shift toward defined, safety-testable tasks rather than undefined "all-knowing"                       
systems[^10.5210_fm.v29i4.13636]. Furthermore, global research trajectories are being closely monitored, with  
specific national strategies explicitly targeting leadership in general AI capabilities by                     
2030[^10.51593_20210064].                                                                                      
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
                                                                                                               
